vember 13. The normal high for the date is 42\u00b0F, and the record is 64\u00b0F (2025). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was the 8th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 131 since 1893.","t_rec":"Glasgow has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Glasgow's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Glasgow has set <strong class=\"sig\">22 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 76 that chance alone would give, and <strong>83 record highs</strong>, close to the 76 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (51). Glasgow's all-time high is 113\u00b0F, on July 31, 1900.","t_chg":"Glasgow's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 119 complete years: Glasgow's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.52\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.42 to +0.62), about +6.8\u00b0F since 1894. Glasgow's average high shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.08 to +0.18) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Glasgow's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.05 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 13.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (22.95 in); the driest, 2021 (6.62 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}